A||||3||Songman||electric trunk release||||5||
Z||000000||Songman||08-11-2001||09:59 PM||||From what I have been told, these are supposed to work without the key being on, and will also work when the engine is running IF the emergency brake is engaged.<P>The one on my Indy does not work without the key being on, and will work with the engine running regardless of the emergency brake being on or off.<P>It is kind of a pain to have to turn the key on to pop the trunk. Any ideas?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||08-11-2001||11:18 PM||||I would look under the dash, for some "home-made" wiring. Sounds like a previous owners version of "theft-lock." Actually sounds like a good idea. I might do that to mine, hmmm...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||08-12-2001||12:20 AM||||I specifically rewired mine to only work with the key on. (Automatic tranny, notes in my cave.) This keeps some jackass from reaching in an open window/sunroof and hitting the release. Also eliminates posibility of anyone (children) easily getting trapped in there. Also means someone who broke into the car has to break the ignition or trunk lock to get anything out of there.<P>It's a bit annoying at times but I'd rather have the extra security. <p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 08-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Songman||08-12-2001||12:29 AM||||Yeah.. I guess that is true...<P>Just hope no one hits the button while I am going down the road! hehe<P>Luckily that big ole spoiler on the back will keep the decklid closed anyway!<P>Thanks guys!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
